    {
      "slug": "05_reddit-wifi-mooching-neighbor",
      "script": "Free Wi-Fi for two years? My neighbor bragged at a cookout that he'd used my default password the whole time, then said I owed him for the security lesson. I finally learned my router settings for the first time. Instead of changing the password, I moved his device to the guest network and capped it at one megabit per second. He kept the free Wi-Fi—technically. His video calls froze. His smart TV buffered every show. Three days later he texted, asking if my internet was broken too. I said mine was great. Then he asked for my real password like a tenant asking a landlord. I promised to look into it and left the cap untouched. Within the week, he bought his own internet plan. Still think the default password was free?",
      "editor_note": "Tightened to 132 words, added a five-word question hook, accelerated the router-cap payoff, and ended on the default-password irony without changing claims or shot structure."
    },
